Article 2 (Types of and Procedures for Revenue-Producing Business)
(1) The Korea Institute of Ocean Science and Technology (hereinafter referred to as "KIOST") may conduct the following revenue-producing businesses pursuant to Article 12 (1) of the Korea Institute of Ocean Science and Technology Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"): <Amended on March 24, 2013>
1. Provision of information relating to ocean science and technology;
2. Technical consulting relating to ocean science and technology;
3. Leasing facilities or equipment of KIOST;
4. Production and sale of publications or programs relating to ocean science and technology;
5. Production and sale of souvenirs relating to ocean science and technology;
6. Other business deemed necessary by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries for achieving the objectives of KIOST or procuring expenses.
(2) Where KIOST intends to commence, modify, or discontinue revenue-producing business under paragraph (1), it shall report thereon in advance to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries. <Amended on March 24, 2013>
(3) Detailed matters necessary for the scope of revenue-producing business and the reporting procedures under paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries. <Amended on March 24, 2013>
